WEBVTT

00:01.001 --> 00:02.877
TENSHIKI

00:02.961 --> 00:05.255
He'd never heard the word "tenshiki."

00:05.338 --> 00:07.799
He should've just asked right away,
but this monk...

00:07.882 --> 00:09.092
Akane!

00:09.175 --> 00:10.719
Isn't it time to get up?

00:10.802 --> 00:12.220
You're going to be late!

00:13.388 --> 00:14.264
Oh, crap!

00:17.017 --> 00:19.227
- Akane!
- See you later!

01:54.531 --> 01:57.617
FIFTH STORY
HER PATH FORWARD

01:57.700 --> 01:58.368
YEAR 3, CLASS 2

01:58.451 --> 02:02.372
All right, I'm going to return your
midterms from the other day now.

02:02.455 --> 02:03.623
- Ms. Adachi.
- Yes.

02:05.583 --> 02:06.626
- Mr. Uchida.
- Yes.

02:07.544 --> 02:09.129
- Mr. Ehara.
- Yes.

02:09.921 --> 02:11.339
- Ms. Osaki.
- Yes.

02:12.966 --> 02:14.300
- Mr. Ozaki.
- Yes.

02:20.265 --> 02:21.474
Thank goodness!

02:21.558 --> 02:23.726
My scores weren't as bad as I thought!

02:23.810 --> 02:26.396
Lisa and Yuka, I owe you one! Thanks!

02:26.479 --> 02:30.150
I mean really, Akane, you were
this close to flunking your finals!

02:30.233 --> 02:31.985
The Mom Blowup Incident.

02:32.068 --> 02:35.989
Actually, there's someone even
more terrifying than Mom now.

02:38.658 --> 02:40.702
Then wanna go celebrate with sweets?

02:40.785 --> 02:41.995
I'm in! I'm in!

02:42.078 --> 02:45.248
Uh, no. Akane, have you forgotten?

02:45.331 --> 02:46.166
Huh?

02:48.209 --> 02:49.210
CAREER COUNSELING ROOM

02:49.294 --> 02:50.128
Ms. Osaki.

02:50.712 --> 02:53.882
You forgot about your
interview today, didn't you?

02:53.965 --> 02:55.925
Oh, well.

02:56.009 --> 02:57.468
You're the only one, you know.

02:57.552 --> 02:59.929
Who hasn't turned in
their career path survey.

03:00.013 --> 03:01.639
What? For real?

03:01.723 --> 03:03.141
Don't be so careless.

03:03.224 --> 03:04.851
Right. I'm sorry.

03:05.768 --> 03:08.354
About your mid-term scores...

03:09.522 --> 03:12.483
You put in a lot of effort.
Not a single F to be seen.

03:12.567 --> 03:15.111
That's right, I did!
I really hit the books this time!

03:15.194 --> 03:16.112
I see.

03:16.195 --> 03:19.115
Meaning you've never
hit the books till now?

03:19.198 --> 03:21.326
Oh, no, um... I'm sorry.

03:23.244 --> 03:26.122
These are the colleges you currently
have the grades to apply to.

03:26.205 --> 03:28.333
Oh, no need to worry about that.

03:29.000 --> 03:31.461
I'm going to become a Rakugoka.

03:31.544 --> 03:33.713
So I won't be going to college,
nor be getting a job.

03:37.842 --> 03:40.178
I see. Very well, then.

03:40.762 --> 03:43.681
All right, let me find
which colleges you have a chance

03:43.765 --> 03:45.850
of getting into
that also have Rakugo clubs.

03:46.559 --> 03:49.437
- No, but, I just said I'm not--
- Ms. Osaki.

03:50.104 --> 03:52.023
Let me be clear about this.

03:52.106 --> 03:54.150
Neither going to college,
nor getting a job

03:54.234 --> 03:55.610
will bring uncertainty into your future.

03:56.361 --> 04:00.073
Not only that, but a career in an obscure
profession like Rakugo...

04:01.574 --> 04:04.535
Iwashimizu-sensei, have you ever seen
a Rakugo performance?

04:04.619 --> 04:06.663
- No, I haven't.
- In that case...

04:06.746 --> 04:07.914
FUTATSUME SHOW - RAKUGO CAFÉ
KYOJI ARAKAWA / KENBISHI ARAKAWA

04:07.997 --> 04:09.540
Here. It's tomorrow!

04:09.624 --> 04:11.376
- If you can--
- Ms. Osaki.

04:11.960 --> 04:17.298
What you need to submit is not a flyer
for an event, but your career path survey.

04:17.382 --> 04:19.133
B-But I...

04:19.217 --> 04:24.013
Here are the brochures for colleges
meeting the criteria I just mentioned.

04:24.722 --> 04:29.102
Take a look at them, and turn in your
career path survey by the end of the week.

04:31.020 --> 04:33.398
I'll just be writing in "Rakugoka."

04:34.023 --> 04:38.486
In that case, I'll be happy to offer you
one-on-one counseling after class

04:38.569 --> 04:40.697
until you can choose a college.

04:45.994 --> 04:48.288
Whoa, how crazy is this?

04:48.371 --> 04:49.622
Was Iwa-sensei being serious?

04:50.373 --> 04:51.749
She was being serious, all right.

04:51.833 --> 04:54.335
I wouldn't put it past that Ice Lady.

04:54.419 --> 04:58.089
If she wipes out my after-school hours,
I'll have no time left for training!

04:58.881 --> 05:01.134
What's that look on your face?

05:01.217 --> 05:03.845
Did Iwa-sensei rip you a new one
during counseling?

05:03.928 --> 05:05.430
Is that you, Jumbo?

05:05.930 --> 05:07.098
Did you have an interview, too?

05:07.181 --> 05:08.599
Mine's tomorrow.

05:08.683 --> 05:10.018
I've got club activities now.

05:10.101 --> 05:12.270
Is that right?

05:12.353 --> 05:13.229
Hey, listen.

05:13.313 --> 05:17.942
Both your parents and your master are
fine with you choosing Rakugo, right?

05:18.526 --> 05:21.946
Then there's no reason to worry,
no matter what anyone says, right?

05:22.947 --> 05:24.198
What's with that face?

05:24.282 --> 05:28.244
Seriously, you grew up
to be a wonderful young man, Jumbo!

05:28.328 --> 05:29.787
I can't believe you're that same kid

05:29.871 --> 05:32.457
who used to cry crocodile tears
in grade school!

05:32.540 --> 05:35.501
Hey, you!
Didn't I tell you to never bring that up?

05:35.585 --> 05:37.628
Starting judo was definitely
the right move!

05:37.712 --> 05:39.380
Look, who do you think you are?

05:46.763 --> 05:48.306
Hey, thanks.

05:48.389 --> 05:50.892
You reached out to me
out of concern, right?

05:51.809 --> 05:53.102
I'll be just fine.

05:53.686 --> 05:55.605
My becoming a Rakugoka...

05:55.688 --> 05:58.274
I'll get Iwa-sensei to accept it!

06:07.450 --> 06:09.911
Easier said than done.

06:09.994 --> 06:12.747
We're talking about Iwa-sensei, after all.

06:12.830 --> 06:15.166
I wonder how you can convince her?

06:15.249 --> 06:17.919
If I go head-to-head with her,
she'll just shoot me down!

06:18.002 --> 06:19.837
Then use your leverage over her to attack.

06:19.921 --> 06:20.755
Scary!

06:20.838 --> 06:23.633
And actually, she's got
way too much leverage over me.

06:23.716 --> 06:26.636
Then why don't you cozy up to her instead?

06:26.719 --> 06:28.387
- Great idea, huh?
- With the Ice Lady?

06:28.471 --> 06:30.098
Not happening, huh?

06:30.181 --> 06:32.141
That's it! Good one, Lisa!

06:32.642 --> 06:34.185
Knowing your opponent's feelings,

06:34.268 --> 06:36.479
and closing the distance
is also attentiveness!

06:36.562 --> 06:40.108
I'll show her the fruits of my training,
and then Iwa-sensei and I will become...

06:40.191 --> 06:41.526
besties for sure!

06:41.609 --> 06:43.986
Sh-She's on fire!

06:48.616 --> 06:49.742
Yes?

06:50.451 --> 06:51.661
Excuse me!

06:51.744 --> 06:53.079
Oh, Iwashimizu-sensei!

06:53.162 --> 06:55.123
Are you just about to have lunch?

06:55.206 --> 06:57.250
What is it, Ms. Osaki?

06:57.333 --> 06:59.877
Would it be all right if I joined you?

07:01.712 --> 07:02.839
Wow!

07:02.922 --> 07:05.049
Your lunch is gorgeous!

07:05.133 --> 07:07.677
Do you make your lunches yourself?

07:08.803 --> 07:11.973
- Yes.
- That's amazing! You're a good cook!

07:12.056 --> 07:13.891
Do you have like, a specialty dish?

07:17.145 --> 07:18.563
Simmered dishes, perhaps.

07:18.646 --> 07:20.314
Really?

07:20.398 --> 07:22.150
That was a good meal!

07:22.233 --> 07:23.443
That was fast.

07:23.526 --> 07:25.862
So, do you have a hobby?

07:27.613 --> 07:31.075
I wouldn't call it a hobby, exactly,
but I'm fond of reading.

07:31.159 --> 07:33.286
Oh, I love reading, too!

07:33.369 --> 07:34.996
Books are great, don't you think?

07:35.079 --> 07:36.706
Reading them on my smartphone is nice,

07:36.789 --> 07:38.666
but the feel of paper
and the smell of ink...

07:38.749 --> 07:39.584
Is that right?

07:40.168 --> 07:43.588
Have you read anything
you found interesting lately?

07:44.922 --> 07:47.633
Oh, crap.
All I read are manga or Rakugo books.

07:48.217 --> 07:49.844
Um...

07:51.387 --> 07:52.513
KENJI MIYAZAWA: THE COMPLETE COLLECTION
VOLUME 12

07:52.597 --> 07:53.764
Kenji Miyazawa!

07:54.515 --> 07:57.477
Like, that was really good!

07:57.560 --> 07:59.479
Which one of Kenji's books?

07:59.562 --> 08:02.064
Huh? Let's see.

08:02.148 --> 08:05.151
Night on the Galactic... Railroad?
And stuff.

08:05.234 --> 08:07.487
Which part of that story
did you find interesting?

08:07.570 --> 08:12.116
Oh, uh, the railroad... on a galactic night...

08:12.200 --> 08:14.202
going boooo! And so on.

08:14.285 --> 08:18.789
What did you think of Giovanni's feelings
for Campanella?

08:18.873 --> 08:23.503
Huh? Giovan... Huh? Huh?

08:24.962 --> 08:26.964
So you haven't read it.

08:27.048 --> 08:29.717
No, I'm sorry.

08:32.136 --> 08:35.348
Ms. Osaki, you like Rakugo, don't you?

08:36.265 --> 08:37.642
Yes! I like it!

08:38.893 --> 08:41.521
Is Rakugo that alluring?

08:41.604 --> 08:42.980
Well, of course!

08:43.064 --> 08:47.276
Being able to create a whole world armed
with just a seat cushion and your words...

08:47.360 --> 08:48.986
All kinds of characters appear,

08:49.070 --> 08:51.781
and you have them move around,
one after another like magic.

08:51.864 --> 08:54.700
The awesomeness of being able to make
people laugh, cry, and get drawn in!

08:55.284 --> 08:59.789
The characters who appear in Rakugo
are all ordinary people just like us.

08:59.872 --> 09:03.668
That's why even if it's an ancient classic
or a different era, you can empathize.

09:03.751 --> 09:08.422
Everything we think or feel in our
daily lives can be used in Rakugo.

09:08.506 --> 09:12.301
Or rather, everything in our daily lives
becomes Rakugo training!

09:12.385 --> 09:14.554
- That aspect is also...
- I see.

09:14.637 --> 09:16.806
Everything you've just done
was part of your plan

09:16.889 --> 09:19.976
to get me to accept that
you want to be a Rakugoka, right?

09:20.560 --> 09:21.519
Let me be clear.

09:22.270 --> 09:24.981
It's useless to try to appease me.

09:25.064 --> 09:27.483
B-Beast you?

09:27.567 --> 09:29.110
As I informed you yesterday,

09:29.193 --> 09:32.113
the deadline for turning in your career
path survey is the end of this week.

09:32.780 --> 09:35.074
I ask that you respect the deadline.

09:39.120 --> 09:41.539
So you went for broke, and broke, huh?

09:41.622 --> 09:43.124
She's got "boulder" in her name.

09:43.207 --> 09:45.543
No, more like partial self-destruction.

09:46.252 --> 09:50.506
Before we could get close, I started
blabbing on and on about Rakugo.

09:51.132 --> 09:52.174
What are you going to do?

09:52.258 --> 09:54.427
Should we come up with another plan?

09:54.510 --> 09:56.012
No.

09:56.095 --> 09:58.472
At this point,
I'll stop with the cheap tricks.

09:58.556 --> 10:02.351
I'll undergo her career counseling
every single day until she accepts it!

10:02.852 --> 10:04.645
- Are you sure?
- Yeah.

10:07.356 --> 10:08.190
CAREER COUNSELING ROOM

10:08.274 --> 10:12.570
Mr. Ozaki, I see that you've been offered
a judo scholarship.

10:12.653 --> 10:16.407
I'll be training under
Coach Saito at Shuei University.

10:16.490 --> 10:17.908
Yes, that's right.

10:17.992 --> 10:20.036
Then let's move forward with that.

10:22.079 --> 10:26.709
Mr. Ozaki, you've known Ms. Osaki
since grade school, right?

10:27.209 --> 10:28.294
Oh, that's right.

10:28.878 --> 10:32.006
I saw you two talking
after her interview yesterday.

10:32.632 --> 10:34.925
Did she seem depressed to you?

10:35.426 --> 10:36.969
Well, maybe a little.

10:37.845 --> 10:40.556
But you don't have to worry.
She'll be fine.

10:40.640 --> 10:42.016
Is that right?

10:42.099 --> 10:44.935
Still, I was a little too harsh on her.

10:45.019 --> 10:46.729
She was acting strangely all day today,

10:47.396 --> 10:50.441
so I should probably have
another proper talk with her.

10:51.734 --> 10:56.238
Iwashimizu-sensei, are you against
Akane becoming a Rakugoka?

10:56.322 --> 10:59.200
That's of no concern to you.

10:59.283 --> 11:00.743
I know it's not.

11:00.826 --> 11:04.872
But it bugs me since
she and I aren't strangers.

11:11.087 --> 11:12.129
That's true.

11:13.089 --> 11:16.884
At the very least,
she's the sociable type.

11:16.967 --> 11:20.262
But she's always zoning out during class,

11:21.013 --> 11:25.476
and I see her muttering some gibberish
and then smirking to herself.

11:25.559 --> 11:27.186
To be honest, I'm worried.

11:27.269 --> 11:28.187
That idiot!

11:29.063 --> 11:30.523
I come across them once in a while.

11:30.606 --> 11:34.151
Students who myopically decide
on their career paths on a whim.

11:34.902 --> 11:36.695
Most likely, she's one of them.

11:36.779 --> 11:39.824
So I have to guide her,
even if it's somewhat forceful.

11:42.701 --> 11:45.079
Hey, you're going to become a Rakugoka?

11:45.162 --> 11:46.914
But your dad...

11:46.997 --> 11:48.082
I've made up my mind.

11:52.878 --> 11:54.547
I've already made up my mind!

11:55.047 --> 11:56.173
FUTATSUME SHOW - RAKUGO CAFÉ
KYOJI ARAKAWA / KENBISHI ARAKAWA

11:56.257 --> 11:58.926
Did you get that flyer from Akane?

11:59.927 --> 12:01.512
I wouldn't say that I got it.

12:01.595 --> 12:03.889
It was more like she pushed it onto me.

12:03.973 --> 12:07.810
Iwashimizu-sensei, would you like
to go to that event with me?

12:07.893 --> 12:09.186
No, thank you.

12:09.270 --> 12:13.023
Spending time with a male student
outside of school

12:13.107 --> 12:15.776
would damage my social standing.

12:15.860 --> 12:17.445
Then we can go separately.

12:18.028 --> 12:22.450
Decide whether she's being myopic
after you've seen her Rakugo.

12:23.576 --> 12:27.496
You certainly seem concerned
about Ms. Osaki.

12:27.580 --> 12:29.707
It's not like that, really.

12:29.790 --> 12:33.961
It's just that I've known her
since grade school.

12:34.545 --> 12:38.674
So I think I know how much
weight Akane's decisions carry.

12:39.717 --> 12:41.802
You're implying something, aren't you?

12:41.886 --> 12:44.930
If it bothers you, then go see her first.

12:45.014 --> 12:48.392
Besides making up your mind
without even seeing her perform?

12:48.476 --> 12:50.936
Isn't that what it means to be myopic?

13:00.070 --> 13:03.282
Years ago, there was a student
in my homeroom

13:03.365 --> 13:06.452
who said his dream
was to become a comedian.

13:09.622 --> 13:10.915
Yes, yes, I hear you.

13:13.125 --> 13:15.878
Oh, it's cold.

13:25.888 --> 13:27.515
IS IT OK IF WE COME OVER TO YOUR HOUSE??

13:27.598 --> 13:30.309
I was supportive of his dream.

13:30.809 --> 13:34.730
I quit the comedians' training school
after six months,

13:34.813 --> 13:36.190
and I'm a part-timer now.

13:36.273 --> 13:39.652
You know, that thing you call talent...

13:39.735 --> 13:41.570
I didn't have any, after all.

13:49.411 --> 13:50.621
Cold.

13:52.748 --> 13:55.084
What could I have done?

13:55.167 --> 13:58.337
Career paths are chosen
by the students themselves.

13:58.963 --> 14:02.258
But I should've done something else
other than just be supportive.

14:02.341 --> 14:07.513
Even if it meant clashing,
I could've told him how I felt.

14:08.138 --> 14:11.559
As a teacher,
I take responsibility for what I say.

14:11.642 --> 14:12.476
RAKUGO CAFÉ 5F

14:12.560 --> 14:14.270
That's what I've decided.

14:19.024 --> 14:22.611
It seemed a little sketchy,
being in a multi-tenant building.

14:23.195 --> 14:24.947
But it looks more proper than I thought.

14:26.407 --> 14:27.908
And there's quite a crowd here.

14:27.992 --> 14:31.745
Oh, my! Are you Akane's friend?

14:31.829 --> 14:32.955
Uh, yes.

14:33.038 --> 14:35.291
So Mr. Ozaki's here, too.

14:35.374 --> 14:38.711
Ma'am, we're ready now.

14:38.794 --> 14:40.129
Okay!

14:40.212 --> 14:42.381
- You have yourself a good time!
- Thank you.

14:43.048 --> 14:47.177
Does Ms. Osaki know
the manager of this café?

14:47.261 --> 14:51.307
Both Ms. Osaki and Mr. Ozaki
were insistent about this event.

14:51.390 --> 14:53.893
What is it that they want to show me?

14:59.773 --> 15:01.150
AKANE

15:06.947 --> 15:08.032
Ms. Osaki?

15:15.915 --> 15:17.666
My name is Akane.

15:18.292 --> 15:20.878
Please join me for a story.

15:23.005 --> 15:24.173
How can this be?

15:24.256 --> 15:26.550
Her name's not on the flyer.

15:26.634 --> 15:28.594
Isn't this a professional gig?

15:29.637 --> 15:31.847
So this is an old story.

15:32.431 --> 15:35.476
There was once a monk at a Buddhist
temple who wasn't feeling well,

15:35.559 --> 15:37.353
and he had the doctor make a house call.

15:37.937 --> 15:42.149
As the doctor was leaving,
"Osho, do you have any tenshiki?"

15:42.232 --> 15:44.068
That's the question he asked the monk.

15:44.151 --> 15:47.571
Now this monk had never heard
of the word "tenshiki."

15:47.655 --> 15:51.241
He should've asked right away,
"What is this 'tenshiki' you speak of?"

15:51.325 --> 15:53.953
But this monk was quite pretentious.

15:54.036 --> 15:56.789
Tenshiki. Ah, tenshiki.

15:58.248 --> 16:00.584
No, I have no tenshiki.

16:01.502 --> 16:02.920
"Tenshiki."

16:03.003 --> 16:06.799
The monk is too proud to admit that
he did not know what tenshiki was.

16:06.882 --> 16:11.637
He sends his apprentice, Chinnen, to find
the meaning of "tenshiki" in his place.

16:11.720 --> 16:14.890
My medicine should be ready by now.

16:14.974 --> 16:17.351
Go over to the doctor's to pick it up.

16:17.434 --> 16:20.479
Oh, and while you're there,
be sure to ask the doctor.

16:20.980 --> 16:23.607
"What exactly is 'tenshiki'?"

16:24.274 --> 16:27.111
Now, no need to say anything like,
"The monk told me to ask."

16:27.194 --> 16:30.406
Ask him the question as if
it came straight from your belly.

16:30.489 --> 16:32.658
Got that? Now run along!

16:32.741 --> 16:34.368
Yes, sir! I'll be on my way.

16:34.451 --> 16:36.954
Hello? Doctor, are you here?

16:37.037 --> 16:39.081
Yes, yes. Ah, it's you, Chinnen.

16:39.164 --> 16:41.291
Right, the medicine is ready.

16:41.375 --> 16:45.254
Have the monk take two measures of this
mixed in with one measure hot water.

16:45.337 --> 16:48.215
Right, thank you very much.

16:48.716 --> 16:50.467
Oh! Excuse me, Doctor.

16:52.094 --> 16:54.930
What is "tenshiki"?

16:55.014 --> 16:58.642
Well, that question certainly
came straight from your belly.

16:58.726 --> 17:00.728
Well, "tenshiki," you see...

17:00.811 --> 17:02.771
In other words, it means "flatulence."

17:02.855 --> 17:05.607
Huh? You mean those things
you use to spread putty around?

17:05.691 --> 17:08.318
No, those are spatulas.
That's not what I mean.

17:08.402 --> 17:10.654
See, what I'm talking about is farts.

17:10.738 --> 17:13.490
I haven't seen Akane's Rakugo in a while,

17:13.574 --> 17:16.076
but she's worked on it
like crazy since then!

17:16.160 --> 17:19.121
"Tenshiki" is written with the characters
"to lose your spirit and fall over."

17:19.204 --> 17:23.250
Well, I guess he felt uncomfortable
asking the monk if he'd been farting.

17:23.333 --> 17:26.003
I was sure that a learned monk
like him would...

17:26.086 --> 17:28.464
What do you think?
That's great footage, right?

17:28.547 --> 17:30.299
- It sucks.
- Huh?

17:30.382 --> 17:31.967
- Just look at that!
- Farting?

17:32.551 --> 17:34.762
Farting, you mean like
what comes out of your butt?

17:34.845 --> 17:36.638
I don't think it comes out
from your mouth much.

17:36.722 --> 17:38.348
A-And it's all yellow?

17:38.432 --> 17:40.225
Well, I wouldn't know about the color.

17:40.309 --> 17:43.312
See? Chinnen's gaze is all over the place.

17:45.022 --> 17:46.815
But it should still be okay, right?

17:46.899 --> 17:47.858
It's not okay.

17:47.941 --> 17:50.486
The audience will be relying
on Chinnen's gaze

17:50.569 --> 17:54.073
to picture the doctor's height,
and the distance between them.

17:54.156 --> 17:55.657
This is no good at all.

17:56.325 --> 17:59.119
It all looks so different
when you're being watched!

17:59.203 --> 18:01.872
- One more time! Just one last time!
- Sure thing.

18:08.128 --> 18:13.467
If I were Akane, I probably
would've ended up hating Rakugo.

18:15.469 --> 18:20.057
That uproar over Akane's dad
getting expelled made the news, as well.

18:20.140 --> 18:23.268
And there was a whole barrage
of criticism aimed at that old geezer.

18:24.728 --> 18:29.233
Meanwhile, Issho Arakawa's Rakugo
started getting tons of attention.

18:33.362 --> 18:36.115
Ethics are no match for emotion.

18:36.198 --> 18:38.242
That criticism morphed
into approval and acclaim,

18:38.325 --> 18:41.537
and some even lauded
the expulsion uproar as legendary.

18:41.620 --> 18:43.247
That even pissed me off.

18:43.831 --> 18:47.209
Even still, Akane chose
to become a Rakugoka.

18:47.292 --> 18:50.337
She wasn't being myopic at all.

18:50.420 --> 18:51.547
Hey, I know!

18:52.214 --> 18:54.091
Why don't I give him
some false information?

18:54.174 --> 18:55.551
Yeah, I will!

18:56.635 --> 18:58.762
Master! I'm back from the doctor's!

18:58.846 --> 19:01.181
Ah, Chinnen. Thanks for your hard work.

19:01.265 --> 19:03.350
Did you ask him the meaning of "tenshiki"?

19:03.433 --> 19:06.103
Oh, yes, I asked him all right!

19:06.687 --> 19:10.190
I found out that by "tenshiki,"
he meant a sake cup!

19:10.274 --> 19:12.568
Sake cup? Sake cup.

19:12.651 --> 19:13.861
Really?

19:13.944 --> 19:15.112
Oh, I see.

19:15.779 --> 19:18.657
If you write "mouth"
under the character "heaven,"

19:18.740 --> 19:19.950
it does become the character "to drink."

19:20.617 --> 19:22.661
"Shi" must be "shu," or "sake."

19:22.744 --> 19:24.538
"Ki" would be "vessel."

19:24.621 --> 19:26.790
A vessel for drinking sake. Tenshiki!

19:26.874 --> 19:28.375
Oh, now I see.

19:28.458 --> 19:31.879
Now look here, Chinnen, I'm sure that
I once taught you that word.

19:31.962 --> 19:35.215
Every day, I stand in front
of the classroom, so I understand.

19:36.091 --> 19:37.551
How nervous you feel
speaking in front of others.

19:38.552 --> 19:40.762
How hard it is to convey
something to others.

19:40.846 --> 19:42.598
Doctor, thanks to your medicine,
I feel much better now!

19:42.681 --> 19:45.559
Ah, is that right?
I'm very glad to hear that.

19:45.642 --> 19:48.520
With only her voice and body,
and only through speech...

19:49.271 --> 19:52.232
I'm embarrassed to say this,
but I happen to love tenshiki, you see.

19:52.316 --> 19:55.277
Y-You love it? Tenshiki?

19:55.944 --> 19:57.446
Making her audience laugh.

19:58.363 --> 20:00.949
It's not an art
that can be mastered overnight.

20:01.033 --> 20:06.413
Today, I'd like to show you
some of this temple's cherished tenshiki.

20:06.496 --> 20:08.457
Uh, no! Th-That won't be necessary!

20:08.540 --> 20:13.545
I had just assumed that this goal
of becoming a Rakugoka

20:13.629 --> 20:15.255
was only a fleeting whim.

20:15.339 --> 20:18.508
That she, too, was a relentless dreamer.

20:18.592 --> 20:20.802
My, my. What magnificent
sake cups these are.

20:20.886 --> 20:23.722
No, no, they're just some shabby tenshiki!

20:24.514 --> 20:26.350
...making up your mind
without even seeing her perform?

20:26.433 --> 20:29.853
Isn't that what it means to be myopic?

20:30.896 --> 20:32.481
You were absolutely right, weren't you?

20:32.564 --> 20:35.359
Chinnen! Telling me such a lie.

20:35.442 --> 20:37.319
Aren't you ashamed of yourself?

20:37.402 --> 20:38.612
No.

20:39.196 --> 20:40.781
It's just a fart in a windstorm to me.

20:47.704 --> 20:49.581
I have a long way to go myself.

20:53.168 --> 20:54.670
CAREER COUNSELING ROOM

20:54.753 --> 20:55.587
I see.

20:55.671 --> 20:56.505
CAREER PATH SURVEY
RAKUGOKA

20:56.588 --> 20:58.340
So you're being true to your word.

20:58.924 --> 21:02.052
Yes! I'm ready to undergo as many
hours of counseling as you want!

21:02.844 --> 21:05.430
- Don't you have any misgivings?
- Misgivings?

21:06.014 --> 21:08.475
Merely lacking a college degree
will narrow down

21:08.558 --> 21:11.603
your options when you're searching
for a job.

21:12.354 --> 21:14.564
The path that you chose
so you can realize your dream

21:15.148 --> 21:17.609
might one day end up making you suffer.

21:18.110 --> 21:22.155
Can you still tell me it doesn't matter,
and that you have zero misgivings?

21:23.448 --> 21:26.326
Yes! It's just a fart in a windstorm.

21:27.577 --> 21:29.037
A foolish question on my part, I see.

21:29.705 --> 21:31.290
I will accept
your career path survey form.

21:32.249 --> 21:35.002
- Don't forget to thank Mr. Ozaki later.
- Huh?

21:35.877 --> 21:39.673
Your Rakugo yesterday
broadened my horizons.

21:40.257 --> 21:41.675
Hey, I knew it!

21:41.758 --> 21:44.094
You were there
at the Rakugo Café yesterday!

21:44.845 --> 21:47.889
This is a flyer
for a student Rakugo competition.

21:47.973 --> 21:49.558
It had been sent to our school, as well.

21:50.392 --> 21:52.811
It never hurts to have achievements
under your belt.

21:52.894 --> 21:54.313
Would you like to take part in it?

21:54.396 --> 21:55.439
KARAKU CUP

21:55.522 --> 21:57.316
This year's head judge will be...

21:58.442 --> 22:01.570
none other than Issho Arakawa.

23:36.248 --> 23:37.999
NEXT EPISODE
TERAKOYA

23:38.875 --> 23:40.669
Akane Small Talk!

23:44.422 --> 23:47.300
You have to think about
the height of your gaze, too?

23:47.384 --> 23:48.802
Rakugo sure is tough.

23:48.885 --> 23:49.970
Oh, not really.

23:50.053 --> 23:52.305
Once you learn the rules,
it's actually easy!

23:52.389 --> 23:53.223
The rules?

23:53.306 --> 23:57.435
For example, in Rakugo, you look
to the right or left when you talk, right?

23:58.854 --> 24:00.147
That's called "Kamishimo wo Kiru."

24:01.022 --> 24:03.900
Someone who comes up to you is on
this side, and they speak facing this way.

24:04.568 --> 24:05.527
The person inside the house,

24:05.610 --> 24:08.989
in other words, the person meeting you
at the door, speaks facing this way.

24:09.072 --> 24:10.365
That's the rule.

24:10.448 --> 24:12.576
Really? That's how it works?

24:12.659 --> 24:14.995
If you look at a kabuki stage, it's clear.

24:15.078 --> 24:16.163
From the audience's perspective,

24:16.246 --> 24:18.915
the hanamichi is on the left side,
which is the "shimote,"

24:18.999 --> 24:21.543
and there are buildings
on the right side, the "kamite."

24:21.626 --> 24:24.087
The person who enters
always comes from the shimote,

24:24.171 --> 24:26.298
while the person meeting them
is on the kamite side.

24:26.381 --> 24:28.091
I get it.

24:28.175 --> 24:31.553
So you can convey all kinds of things
with your face or gaze.

24:31.636 --> 24:32.637
Right!

24:32.721 --> 24:35.682
Whether that person
is inside the house, or outside,

24:35.765 --> 24:39.311
or if they're taller or shorter
than the other, and also...

24:39.394 --> 24:41.021
Straight above?

24:41.104 --> 24:42.856
When would you look that way?

24:42.939 --> 24:44.065
When I lose track of my material!

24:44.149 --> 24:46.234
Hey, you gotta memorize that stuff!
